  "investigation_notes": "Uploads are failing because the upload storage filesystem is full.\n\n**Root cause: `/srv/lab-data` capacity exhausted - `No space left on device` on write**\n\n* App `POST /upload` returns `500 Internal Server Error` with `OSError: [Errno 28] No space left on device` in `upload` at `out.write(chunk)` (E5).\n* Filesystem holding `/srv/lab-data` is `99.9%` used with `0.4 MB` available (E3).\n* Low inodes are ruled out: `inode_use_percent` is `0.3%` (E3), so this is capacity exhaustion, not inode exhaustion.\n* Isolation to that mount: root `/` filesystem is `6.8%` used with `91424.2 MB` available (E6), while `/srv/lab-data` is its own mountpoint (E3) bind-mounted to `/data` in `incidentlab-app-1` `rw: true` (E8).\n* Permissions ruled out: `/srv/lab-data/uploads` (E4) and `/srv/lab-data` (E11) are `owner 1000:1000 mode 0755` with `app_uid 1000` and `app_user_can_write: true`.\n* Dependency ruled out: `incidentlab-db-1` is `running` `healthy` (E1)(E10), logs show `database system is ready to accept connections` with no errors (E9), and recent events show `health_status: healthy` (E7).\n* App crash ruled out: `incidentlab-app-1` is `running` (E1)(E8) with `/health` returning `200 {\"status\":\"ok\"}` (E2). Earlier `POST /upload 200 OK` lines in (E5) show uploads worked before the `ENOSPC` failure.\n\nSymptom is the `500` on `/upload` (E5); root cause is storage full on `/srv/lab-data` (E3).\n",
